.TH FRDP-SESMAND 8 "July 2026" "FreeRDP" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
frdp-sesmand \- managed PAM session service for frdpd
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B frdp-sesmand
.RB [ --pam-service " " name " | " --config " " path ]
.BI --socket " absolute-path"
.PP
.B frdp-sesmand
.BI --pam-service " name"
.BI --open-session " user"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B frdp-sesmand
verifies authorization tokens from
.BR frdp-authd (8),
owns PAM session handles, starts per-user
.BR frdp-session-agent (8)
processes, and exposes session list, detach, reconnect, close, and reload
operations over a local Unix-domain socket.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --pam-service " name"
Select the PAM service directly.
.TP
.BI --config " path"
Read PAM, resource-limit, display-backend, and heartbeat policy from the FRDP configuration.
.TP
.BI --socket " absolute-path"
Listen on the specified Unix-domain socket.
.TP
.BI --open-session " user"
Run the standalone development session path.  This requires
.B FRDP_SESMAND_ALLOW_STANDALONE=1
and is not the normal service topology.
.TP
.B --help
Show command usage.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FRDP_AUTH_TOKEN_KEY
Path to the owner-only shared authorization-token key.
.TP
.B FRDP_SESMAND_ALLOW_STANDALONE
Set to 1 to permit the explicit development-only standalone path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR frdpd (8),
.BR frdp-authd (8),
.BR frdp-session-agent (8),
.BR frdpctl (1)
